    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "@Haroenv Not really, it can fail when the first tag found is undefined. You can fix it this way:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nconst [ { description = 'other' } = {} ] = filter(s.tags, { title: 'category' });\r\nreturn description;\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd even this can fail if the first tag found is not an object or not undefined. I would not recommend to go this far in object destructuring if your are not sure of the result.\r\n\r\nAnd in the end, when you transpile with babel it will produce more code than needed. For example this will be the transpile of the example I provided in my first comment:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfunction foo() {\r\n  var _filter3 = filter(s.tags, { title: 'category' }),\r\n      _filter4 = _slicedToArray(_filter3, 1),\r\n      tag = _filter4[0];\r\n\r\n  return tag && tag.description || 'other';\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnd then compare with the second example I provided (similar as the one you shared):\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfunction foo() {\r\n  var _filter = filter(s.tags, { title: 'category' }),\r\n      _filter2 = _slicedToArray(_filter, 1),\r\n      _filter2$ = _filter2[0];\r\n\r\n  _filter2$ = _filter2$ === undefined ? {} : _filter2$;\r\n  var _filter2$$description = _filter2$.description,\r\n      description = _filter2$$description === undefined ? 'other' : _filter2$$description;\r\n\r\n  return description;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI recommend you to try out this kind of stuff into the https://babeljs.io/repl/ 👍 ",
    "commit_id": "7a2f722063e162b3e306c17a7653107184018a3b",
    "created_at": "2017-08-01T13:30:27Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -70,8 +72,14 @@ function filterSymbolsByType(type, symbols) {\n   });\n }\n \n+function groupSymbolsByCategories(symbols) {\n+  return groupBy(symbols, (s) => {\n+    const tag = filter(s.tags, {title: 'category'})[0];\n+    return tag && tag.description || 'other';",
